    "https://lesley.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/Lesley_University_Careers/job/Cambridge-MA/Assistant-Director-of-Admissions-and-Events-Coordinator_JR101665-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Admissions",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nThe Opportunity Lesley University is seeking an Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions to join our Enrollment team. Working collaboratively with the Vice President of Enrollment, Associate Vice President of Enrollment, and reporting to the Senior Associate Director of Admissions, this position will play an important role in advancing undergraduate recruitment efforts and supporting the university’s enrollment goals. The Assistant Director will oversee an assigned recruitment territory, developing meaningful relationships with prospective students, families, school counselors, and community partners. This role will require regular travel to regional and national recruitment events, high school visits, college fairs, and other enrollment activities. The Assistant Director will also evaluate applications for admission to Lesley’s undergraduate programs and contribute to shaping a thoughtful, student-centered admission process. The successful candidate will be a collaborative team member who works closely with colleagues across the Enrollment Department and builds strong partnerships with campus offices to support recruitment, yield, and student success initiatives. This position will have the opportunity to contribute to strategic enrollment initiatives while taking ownership of projects that support the university’s continued growth. Additional responsibilities and special projects will be assigned by senior leadership as needed.   Qualities and Capabilities  The successful candidate will have:  Bachelor’s degree required. Superior written, verbal, and public speaking communication skills. Represent Lesley University at various recruitment events such as high school visits, college fairs, and community college visits as needed. Plan, manage, and conduct recruitment travel, and counseling activities targeting prospective students and influencers (parents, school counselors, professors) and other major stakeholders in the college search process. Demonstrated ability to contribute to enrollment goals through effective recruitment strategies, territory management, relationship building, and engagement with prospective students, families, and school/community partners. Oversee the yield process for assigned territory for admitted students. Responsible for daily follow-up, communication, and advising of students through the enrollment process. Build and maintain strong relationships with strategic high schools, secondary school counselors, independent counselors, prospective students, families, and Lesley alumni to support recruitment efforts, enhance engagement, and strengthen enrollment pathways. Effectively present marketing messages and accurate academic information on all undergraduate programs leading to positive and informed decision-making regarding the fit between students and Lesley University. Demonstrated cross-cultural competence and the ability to communicate effectively with students and families from diverse backgrounds. Deliver engaging public presentations both on and off campus to prospective students, families, and other audiences about Lesley’s undergraduate programs. Presentations may range in size from small groups of 10 to larger audiences of 150+ participants and may occasionally require evening, weekend (Saturday and Sunday), or select Monday holiday commitments. Assist with planning and coordinating daily campus tours to ensure an exceptional visitor experience, with a focus on personalized engagement, attention to detail, and creating a welcoming environment for prospective students and families. Develop and maintain meaningful relationships with prospective students, teachers, high school guidance counselors, independent educational consultants, alumni admissions volunteers, and parents through a variety of communication channels, including phone, email, social media, and web-based applications. Review applications, portfolios and recommend decisions. Manage databases and input data using a CRM, Colleague, Microsoft Word, and Excel. 1-3 years’ experience working in higher education and/or customer service settings. Valid U.S driver’s license. Why Lesley Located in the heart of Cambridge, Massachusetts, Lesley University is highly regarded for its graduate and undergraduate programs in the human arts of education, the arts, and applied social sciences. Lesley fosters a highly creative environment in which innovative ideas thrive, theory is integrated with practice and its 6,400 students and 90,000 alumni are empowered to improve and enrich communities. We offer a competitive benefits package that includes health, dental, life, and long-term disability insurance. In addition, we offer significant paid time off, a generous retirement plan, and tuition programs that enable employees and their dependents to expand their knowledge and skills. Lesley is committed to the ongoing pursuit of strategic diversity initiatives that help to position diversity, equity, and inclusion as fundamental to institutional and academic excellence at Lesley. In doing so, Lesley strives for a campus culture and community that fosters a true sense of belonging for all, provides opportunity for everyone to participate equally and fully in the Lesley experience, and helps to develop each individual's capacity to confidently and competently engage within and across difference. Given an evolving national context and the rapid change in the demographic profile of our country, the University has made a significant commitment to addressing and enhancing its campus climate and diversity capabilities as an institution. Expressing Interest A letter of interest, CV/resume, and a statement addressing past and/or potential contributions to diversity, equity, and inclusion through teaching, professional activity, and/or service must be included for full consideration. At Lesley University we strive for a supportive and equitable environment where people -- regardless of race, ethnicity, color, sex, physical ability, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, neurodiversity, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, veteran or military status, membership in uniformed services, and all other categories protected by applicable state and federal laws -- can participate equally and fully as their true selves in all aspects of university life. Accordingly, the University prohibits discrimination based on these protected categories in any education program or activity that it operates, including in admission and in employment. We are committed to diversity, equity, and inclusion throughout the fabric of our institution. Individuals may submit concerns or questions related to discrimination to the University's Director of Equal Opportunity. Please visit the Office of Equal Opportunity's webpage for the University's entire notice of nondiscrimination and for additional information. Base Pay Range: $59,536 - $66,761 annually"
    },
    "https://lesley.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/Lesley_University_Careers/job/No-Office-Location/Adjunct-Faculty---Mathematics--Evergreen-_JR101648-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty – Mathematics (Evergreen)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nPart time\n\nThe Opportunity Lesley University always welcomes applications for Adjunct Faculty to teach upcoming classes in our Mathematics programs at the undergraduate level. These programs include classes in Algebra, Calculus, Geometry, and Statistics. Most classes are taught in-person, with occasional availability for remote courses. Lesley University hires Adjunct Faculty on a regular cadence to support our Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. By applying to an Evergreen position, your materials will remain on file and be reviewed on an as-needed basis throughout the upcoming semesters. As such, you will be put into consideration for current and future adjunct positions within the Mathematics subject areas. The specific course hired for is subject to change depending on semester, course catalog, and department needs. About Liberal Arts & Business Lesley’s Liberal Arts & Business programs offer a broad foundation for all students. With 13 undergraduate majors across Business, Humanities, Natural Sciences, and Social Sciences, our graduates leave Lesley ready to take on diverse careers in education, business, human services, science, the arts, and more. Anchored by our outcomes-driven CommonLynx general education curriculum, our programs feature ​​innovative role-play-based teaching, flexible specializations, and the opportunity to build skills and gain real-world experience through ​​guaranteed internships. Qualities & Capabilities A successful candidate will have: Master's degree in Mathematics or a closely related field; (required); PhD or terminal degree (preferred) Successful experience teaching in the particular discipline at the undergraduate level Experience in constructivist, inquiry-based learning with an emphasis on student Why Lesley Located in the heart of Cambridge, Massachusetts, Lesley University is highly regarded for its graduate and undergraduate programs in the human arts of education, the arts, and applied social sciences. Lesley fosters a highly creative environment in which innovative ideas thrive, theory is integrated with practice and its 6,400 students and 90,000 alumni are empowered to improve and enrich communities.   Lesley is committed to the ongoing pursuit of strategic diversity initiatives that help to position diversity, equity, and inclusion as fundamental to institutional and academic excellence at Lesley. In doing so, Lesley strives for a campus culture and community that fosters a true sense of belonging for all, provides opportunity for everyone to participate equally and fully in the Lesley experience, and helps to develop each individual's capacity to confidently and competently engage within and across difference. Given an evolving national context and the rapid change in the demographic profile of our country, the University has made a significant commitment to addressing and enhancing its campus climate and diversity capabilities as an institution. Expressing Interest A CV/resume which demonstrates teaching experience, professional activity, and/or service must be included for full consideration.   At Lesley University we strive for a supportive and equitable environment where people -- regardless of race, ethnicity, color, sex, physical ability, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, neurodiversity, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, veteran or military status, membership in uniformed services, and all other categories protected by applicable state and federal laws -- can participate equally and fully as their true selves in all aspects of university life. Accordingly, the University prohibits discrimination based on these protected categories in any education program or activity that it operates, including in admission and in employment. We are committed to diversity, equity, and inclusion throughout the fabric of our institution. Individuals may submit concerns or questions related to discrimination to the University's Director of Equal Opportunity. Please visit the Office of Equal Opportunity's webpage for the University's entire notice of nondiscrimination and for additional information. Lesley University Adjunct Faculty positions are governed by a Collective Bargaining Agreement (CBA). To view our compensation targets for this position, please visit this link ."
