      "title": "Adjunct Faculty – Illustration (Evergreen)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-24\nPart time\n\nThe Opportunity    Lesley University always welcomes applications for adjunct faculty to teach upcoming daytime or evening classes for our Illustration programs at the undergraduate level. Subject areas in this department include courses on Illustration and Visual Narrative. Classes in this department are primarily taught in-person and on-campus.  Since adjunct faculty positions are ongoing, evergreen positions, your materials will remain on file and will be reviewed on an as-needed basis throughout the upcoming semesters. By submitting your application, you will be put into consideration for current and future adjunct positions within the undergraduate Illustration subject area. We hire adjunct faculty on a regular cadence to support our Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. The specific course hired for is subject to change depending on semester, course catalog, and department needs.      About Lesley Art & Design   At Lesley Art + Design , students are multidisciplinary artists who shape cultural trends and spark change. As future leaders in their fields, students understand that ideas and implementation are equally important, encompassing both artistic vision and business acumen.  Our undergraduate Bachelor of Fine Arts programs span Communication Arts, Illustration , Media Arts and Studio Arts. We also offer low residency Master of Fine Arts programs in Visual Arts and Creative Writing. Our alumni are always welcomed back to our Alumni Studio co-working space, to create and collaborate on their own projects amongst other Art & Design alumni.  Qualities & Capabilities  Required:  Master's degree in Illustration or related field 2+ years minimum of professional experience working in a related art field Demonstrated successful experience teaching in the particular discipline at the undergraduate level   Experience in studio-based, experiential learning with an emphasis on student engagement  Demonstrated advance